    "created_at": "2016-02-08T09:30:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-21T19:23:34Z",
    "body": "Reading those comments again, the reporter argues that non-void is a benefit because the descendant elements can be styled. But to me that seems like a reason to _not_ do non-void, since we don't support styling, and people will be confused if they assume they can apply styling and it doesn't work.\n\nI suppose we could implement the proposal in this issue, but only allow using the attribute for authoring conformance. That way we can start allowing use of children in the future if we want to somehow start supporting styling.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
